### Refunds 

You can refund Konbini payments through the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md). For detailed information about customer actions, refund statuses, failures, and testing, see [Refund Konbini payments](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/konbini/accept-a-payment.md?payment-ui=direct-api#refunds).

#### Refund process 

Konbini payments are made with cash, so refunds can’t be returned to the original payment source. Instead, Stripe emails your customer to collect their bank account details, then issues the refund as a bank transfer. Your customer must respond to the email and provide their bank information before the refund can be processed.

#### Tracking refunds 

To check a refund’s status, open the payment in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.

Stripe notifies you of the final status through a `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. [Verify webhook signatures](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md#verify-events) to confirm that events came from Stripe. You can also use Stripe’s [public IP addresses](https://docs.stripe.com/ips.md) for network allowlisting. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) status changes to `succeeded`. If the refund fails, the status changes to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your Stripe balance. You must refund the customer using another method.

### Disputes 

Konbini doesn’t support the standard dispute process—customers can’t file chargebacks, and funds aren’t withdrawn from your Stripe balance because of a dispute. In rare cases, a convenience store might report an irregularity, such as payment mishandling. If this happens, Stripe contacts you with next steps.

