1. Only supports send_invoice collection method.
### Hosted invoices 

Customers can pay hosted invoices, including subscription invoices, with Konbini when the invoice or subscription uses `collection_method=send_invoice`. The customer must make a cash payment for each invoice. Konbini doesn’t support automatic charging or Checkout subscription mode.

## Connect 

A Japanese platform can settle destination charges or separate charges and transfers on its own account using its own Konbini activation. In this case, don’t set `on_behalf_of`. The connected account doesn’t need to activate Konbini.

## Customer experience 

#### 1. Select Konbini

The customer selects Konbini at checkout and provides their name and email address. They can optionally provide a phone number as their confirmation number.

#### 2. Receive payment instructions

Stripe displays payment codes, a confirmation number, and an expiration time for each supported convenience-store chain. The customer can view the instructions on desktop or mobile, or print them.

#### 3. Pay at a convenience store

Before the instructions expire, the customer presents the appropriate payment code and confirmation number at a supported convenience store in Japan and pays in cash.

#### 4. Payment complete

The store provides a receipt. Stripe confirms the payment asynchronously, changes the PaymentIntent status to `succeeded`, and notifies you so you can fulfill the order.

### Statement descriptors 

Customers pay for Konbini payments in cash, so the payment doesn’t create an entry on their bank or card statement. Card-style dynamic and account-level statement descriptors don’t appear for the customer payment. Stripe displays a payment code and confirmation number in the payment instructions for each supported store chain. Retrieve these values from `PaymentIntent.next_action.konbini_display_details.stores.<store>.payment_code` and `.confirmation_number`.

These values are payment instructions, not post-payment transaction IDs.

## Enable Konbini 

If you use Stripe front-end products, enable Konbini in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically determines which payment methods are most relevant to each customer.

If your integration requires manually listing payment methods, you can [configure Konbini as an accepted payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/konbini/accept-a-payment.md).
